re \u2014 so it now describes the\n17: file\u002dbased store and says plainly that a memory alone is never enough, since it\n18: lives outside the repo and nobody else reads it.\n19: \n20: **The find worth keeping:** `.githooks/pre\u002dpush` was installed as the relative\n21: `core.hooksPath=.githooks`. That resolves against the working tree being pushed,\n22: and a correctly built `pr/*` branch has no `.githooks/` in it \u2014 removing it is the\n23: point of `git rebase \u002d\u002donto upstream/next`. So the guard was absent from exactly\n24: the branches it guards; both PR worktrees were unguarded and had always been.\n25: Fixed by installing it by absolute path, which every branch can see.\n26: \n27: Six personal paths were also missing from `PERSONAL_PATTERNS` and would have\n28: travelled upstream: `CLAUDE.md`, `.github/sessions/`, and four fork\u002donly tools\n29: (`cloud\u002dtest\u002dbackend`, `cloud\u002dround\u002dtrip`, `lint\u002daudit\u002dartifacts`, `vm\u002dvisual\u002dqa`).\n30: `tools/` is mostly upstream's, so ours have to be enumerated. Added an\n31: unlisted\u002dartifact check that warns on any `next`\u002donly file outside `packages/` and\n32: `projects/` the list does not recognise \u2014 a warning, not a block, because features\n33: merge into `next` before being PR'd, so next\u002donly does not prove personal.\n34: \n35: Verified by construction rather than by absence: a synthetic PR branch carrying\n36: `tools/cloud\u002dtest\u002dbackend` is blocked; with the pattern removed the warning fires\n37: instead; a real clean PR branch passes silently. Registered as blindspot 14 \u2014 a\n38: guard with no observed positive is a guard with no evidence.\n\nTARGET 35 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_26\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 702aa0b4bcdf25e668e5d03a51fbd5b5d324237a 054ecd0866b8dd5218af8ae3991869e3e8ea9ce7d3bd3d958d3dc8b033ab51be RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED []\n1: # Work log \u2014 2026\u002d08\u002d26\n2: \n3: ## The system\u002dbackup phase of cloud sync never restored anything\n4: \n5: Went through the legacy `cloud_backup`/`cloud_restore` (621/664 lines) while\n6: waiting on hardware. Started from the one invariant the rules state \u2014 that the\n7: two scripts stay structurally in sync \u2014 and diffed their shared functions. The\n8: helpers were identical; the drift was all in the phase\u002d2 code, which is where\n9: the bug was.\n10: \n11: `cloud_restore`'s system\u002dbackup phase filtered on `/backup/*.zip` and\n12: `backup/*.zip`, but that transfer's root is `SYNCPATH_BACKUP`, whose contents\n13: came from `BACKUPFOLDER` \u2014 so the archive is at the root, not under `backup/`.\n14: Neither include matched. Because using `\u002d\u002dinclude` at all excludes everything\n15: it does not match, the transfer moved no files, exited 0, and the summary\n16: printed SUCCESS. Shipped in four images. Reachable only for users who set\n17: `BACKUPFILE_RESTORE_OPTION=\"yes\"`, which is off by default.\n18: \n19: The backup side had the same mistake with no symptom: it borrowed the saves\n20: allowlist through `RESTORE_RCLONEOPTS`, whose rules are anchored to\n21: `BACKUPPATH` while that transfer's root is `BACKUPFOLDER`, and whose\n22: `\u002d /**/*.zip` matches the archive. It worked only because rclone applies\n23: `\u002d\u002dinclude` ahead of `\u002d\u002dfilter\u002dfrom`. A precedence detail was the only thing\n24: holding it up.\n25: \n26: **Method worth repeating:** rather than reason about rclone's filter\n27: precedence, I built a fixture tree and asked rclone. That settled four\n28: questions in one pass and caught two excludes that had never matched anything\n29: (`\"${BACKUPFOLDER}/**\"` is absolute where rclone matches relative to the\n30: transfer root; `backups/**` names a directory that does not exist \u2014 it is\n31: `backup`). Then I ran the real scripts end\u002dto\u002dend against the WebDAV test\n32: backend by relocating `/storage` into a scratch tree, and ran the **shipped**\n33: script alongside the fixed one: 4 saves / 0 archives before, 4 / 1 after.\n34: A before\u002dand\u002dafter on the real code is what turns \"I think this was broken\"\n35: into evidence.\n36: \n37: Also fixed: `\u002d\u002dsystem\u002donly` was parsed and ignored by `cloud_restore`, so it\n38: restored game saves over local ones \u2014 the opposite of the flag. \"Nothing to\n39: transfer\" returned 1 in both system phases and printed COMPLETED WITH ERRORS on\n40: a device that had simply never made a backup. `check_internet` pinged\n\nTARGET 36 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_27\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY efa24a1779acd848262642ac089735b9318be341 6b9b78ef31152660af215087eb912469ac4ebd76a741d4c569093c499fa6ae9e RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [15, 16, 17]\n1: # Work log \u2014 2026\u002d08\u002d27\n2: \n3: ## First working backup/restore round\u002dtrip on a device since January\n4: \n5: Built `ROCKNIX\u002dGENERIC_X64.x86_64\u002d20260826` clean (631/631, no failures, ~2h49m)\n6: and ran the full backup/restore round\u002dtrip in QEMU. Everything passed, and this\n7: is the first image on which `backuptool backup` could execute at all \u2014 the\n8: missing `zip` package had made the backup path dead since upstream dropped it\n9: in January.\n10: \n11: **backuptool, on the guest:**\n12: \n13: \u002d `zip` present and running (Info\u002dZIP 3.0), which was the whole point of the rebuild.\n14: \u002d `backuptool backup` completed: 16.4M, 227 entries, `unzip \u002dt` OK.\n15: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n16: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n17: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n18:   as designed for the post\u002drestore re\u002dentry page.\n19: \u002d Archive rotation worked \u2014 the previous backup moved into `backup/archive/`.\n20: \u002d `backuptool restore` verified the archive, restored, set\n21:   `.restore\u002dfinish\u002dpending`, and rebooted. After the reboot all three planted\n22:   settings held their backed\u002dup values (`audio.preamp=77`,\n23:   `display.brightness=33`, `video_fullscreen=\"false\"`), having been mutated to\n24:   11 / 99 / \"true\" beforehand. One\u002dto\u002done match confirmed.\n25: \n26: **cloud, via `tools/cloud\u002dround\u002dtrip` over SSH:** all checks passed, including\n27: the system\u002dbackup archive reaching the cloud and coming back byte\u002didentical \u2014\n28: the phase\u002d2 fix from the 26th, which had never run on a device \u2014 plus saves\n29: round\u002dtripping, the allowlist keeping excluded files out, and content\n30: backup/restore.\n31: \n32: **A test\u002ddesign correction worth keeping.** My first round\u002dtrip attempt replaced\n33: a 225\u002dline OS\u002dmanaged `system.cfg` with a 3\u002dline synthetic file. After restore\n34: and reboot the file had 225 lines again and my planted `wifi.ssid` was gone, which\n35: looked like restore being undone. It was not: boot\u002dtime seeding regenerates keys\n36: that are missing, and I had removed 222 of them. Re\u002drunning against *existing*\n37: keys with distinctive values gave a clean, meaningful pass. A synthetic fixture\n38: that does not resemble the real file tests the fixture, not the feature \u2014 the\n39: same shape as blindspot 8.\n40: \n"
